# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for third-party libraries, used ONLY by the tests that
# execute the Qt application binary (currently tests/cli_check.cmake).
#
# Constructing a QGuiApplication on Linux starts a QDBusConnection worker thread, and
# glib's event loop races with it on its own eventfd -- entirely inside libglib-2.0 and
# libQt6DBus, with no Musa CAD frame anywhere in either stack. It fires with both the
# `offscreen` and `minimal` platform plugins, so it is not something the headless plot
# path can avoid; it is Qt/glib's own noise, the same situation tools/lsan.supp already
# handles for the GUI smoke run.
#
# These are `called_from_lib` entries on purpose: they suppress only reports whose stack
# passes through those libraries. A race in Musa CAD's own code still fails the run --
# the concurrency tests (triple buffer, MPSC queue, engine) are unaffected, and no
# suppression is active for the rest of the suite.
called_from_lib:libglib-2.0.so
called_from_lib:libgio-2.0.so
called_from_lib:libQt6DBus.so
